040000             0002      ; Wolf3D eZ80 client -- the real, growing game application.
040000             0003      ;
040000             0004      ; Distinct from its two siblings under src/asm/: wolf3d_hello (raw wire-
040000             0005      ; protocol smoke test for the BUFFERED_WOLF3D VDP opcode) and wolf3d_ai (the
040000             0006      ; sight/collision logic's own prototyping + regression-test project, whose
040000             0007      ; validated reusable API graduated into this app once that work was done --
040000             0008      ; see wolf3d_world.inc/wolf3d_math.inc/wolf3d_sight.inc below).
040000             0009      ;
040000             0010      ; The original player's-first-position render fixture (Author decision
040000             0011      ; 2026-07-31) has grown into the application shell and complete shareware-floor
040000             0012      ; loader. It loads each floor's real wall/door and static-sprite art through the
040000             0013      ; vendored AGNB loader, uploads the runtime W3L tilemap, and drives the settled
040000             0014      ; BUFFERED_WOLF3D wire protocol with callback-gated rendering. Player collision,
040000             0015      ; eZ80-authoritative moving doors, blocking decorations, and mutable pickup/HUD
040000             0016      ; state are live. The authoritative actor pool advances original-timed path
040000             0017      ; patrols, awareness/reaction, ordinary chase/dodge movement, ranged and dog
040000             0018      ; attack chains, player damage, all four ordinary player weapons, actor pain/
040000             0019      ; death, scores and drops, and the original ordinary death/fizzle/respawn loop.
040000             0020      ; Native-rate digitized combat, pickup, door, and environment effects are
040000             0021      ; loaded through AGNB and arbitrated once per caught-up simulation quantum.
040000             0022      ; Episode 1 floor routing, original-looking floor intermissions, and the E1L9
040000             0023      ; victory return are live. Bosses and the intermission's original count-up/
040000             0024      ; bonus animation are live; paid-episode projectile actors remain future work
040000             0025      ; and are not present in the WL1 maps. Original
040000             0026      ; IMF register streams drive a nonblocking nine-voice VDP music translation.
040000             0027      ; =============================================================================
